      "writtenOn": "2024-09-09T17:16:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Friday (September 13) will be my last working day\n\nOh, too bad for me ;-)\n\nI wish you all the best for the future. Thanks for your help so far!\n\n---\n\n@kjlubick@chromium.org:\n\nCurrently, the absence of Bazel bots with partition_alloc isn\u0027t critical as Skia pointers remain unchanged.  I\u0027ll ensure a clear path forward before proceeding.\n\nI experimented with supporting Bazel in partition_alloc. It was relatively straightforward, with feature flags being the main challenge. I considered hosting BUILD.bazel files from the partition_alloc repository, but hosting everything from Skia (potentially removing feature flag management) might be preferable. I will ask what are Skia developers preference.\n\nIf you\u0027re interested, I\u0027m available for a 1:1 discussion sometime this month to delve deeper.",
